# Vue 3 / TypeScript (dashboard)

Caps: soft **150** / hard **300** lines per SFC or `.ts` module; functions **≤40** lines. Feature views split before hard cap.

## Principles (Context7 / Vue + TS)

- Always `<script setup lang="ts">` for components
- Type props with `defineProps<{ ... }>()`; type emits with `defineEmits<{ event: [payload] }>()` (Vue 3.3+ tuple form)
- Prefer Composition API: `ref` / `computed` / composables — no new Options API
- Keep components presentational when possible; put API/data in `src/api/` + small composables next to views
- `const` by default; narrow with type guards; avoid `any` (use `unknown` + narrow)
- Strict TypeScript — do not weaken `tsconfig` for convenience

## Structure

- `views/` — route screens; `components/` — app chrome; `components/ui/` — shadcn-vue (treat as vendor: wrap, don't bloat)
- `api/` — HTTP clients; `lib/` — pure helpers; `router/` — routes only
- One view ≈ one route concern; extract tables/forms/charts into sibling components when nearing soft cap

## Do / Don't

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
const props = defineProps<{ title: string; count?: number }>()
const emit = defineEmits<{ change: [id: number] }>()
</script>
```

- Do not enlarge `components/ui/**` primitives — compose them from views/feature components
- Prefer existing Tailwind / shadcn-vue patterns over one-off CSS
- Router and API modules stay free of UI markup
